n data loss.\n\n### Carriers off by more than ~1%\n\n**Guardian — report 2,430 enrolled / 72 companies vs. portal 2,403 / 69 groups; $151,848.02 vs. $149,594.41 (−$2,253.61, −1.48%).** This is a company-count difference, not a premium error: the Carrier Stats report counts every company Guardian writes, including archived ones, and the portal only holds $268.21 of archived Guardian premium. Three companies in Guardian's count simply aren't in the XML export — consistent with the parser rejecting Sign Express Inc. dba CSE Graphics (\"no current enrollments\") and with the unfiled Bostrom Seating invoice below. No action needed on the premium figures themselves.\n\nEvery other carrier is inside tolerance (EBPA +0.75%, HealthEZ −0.86%, UNUM −0.85%, BCBS-AL −0.37%, VSP −0.44%); Flores and StreamlineHR carry no premium by design.\n\n### Groups where billing differs from the XML\n\n47 of 65 groups tie exactly. Of the 18 that don't, nearly all differ by one to three participants — normal timing, since the funding period runs 8/15–9/14 while the export is a 9/2 snapshot. Examples: Ingram Equipment (50 → 51), Fetch Freight (16 → 17), Taziki's (173 → 175 billed).\n\nWorth a look:\n- **Johnson Storage & Moving (96 vs. 90 billed, −$3,743.19)** and **Aviation Service Partners (51 vs. 48, −$1,517.74)** — six and three more enrolled in the portal than billed; likely new hires effective after the billing cutoff.\n- **Forestry Environmental (60 vs. 60, −$751.50)** and **Spartan Value Investors (56 vs. 56, −$513.01)** — same headcount, different dollars, which points to a rate change or plan renewal since the export, not an enrollment problem.\n- **Up Accounting (5 vs. 4, −$1,156.09)** and **Wilmer Medical Clinic (7 vs. 5, −$1,107.85)** — small groups where one or two lives swings a third of the premium.\n\n### Unfiled invoice\n\nInvoice 40599, Bostrom Seating (37 lines), matched no group — almost certainly one of the companies missing from the export.\n\n### What to do\n\nConfirm Guardian's three extra companies are archived or terminated groups; assign Bostrom Seating (and Sign Express) or confirm they're intentionally out of the portal; ask EBPA/HealthEZ to confirm the Forestry and Spartan rate changes; and spot-check headcount at Johnson Storage, Aviation Service Partners, Up Accounting and Wilmer. The 620 ended medical lines ($392,367.86) and 9,764 terminated employees were correctly excluded — no follow-up required.","readAt":"2026-09-03T19:10:08.240Z","reading":false}}